        "original_id": "375f321a-5937-50c3-98b1-827271ef2284",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Auty, Mary Plazas\n- Works: La Bohème (2009 film), \"Walking in the Air\", \"O soave fanciulla\", La bohème\n- Places: Ethiopia, Britain, continental Europe\n- Organizations: St Paul's Cathedral, Stiff Records, major opera companies\n\nFacts:\n- Peter Robert Auty was born on 4 November 1969 and is an English operatic tenor.\n- Peter Auty has worked with most major opera companies in Britain and with a number of companies in continental Europe.\n- In the film, \"Walking in the Air\" was performed by St Paul's Cathedral choirboy Peter Auty and was reissued in 1985 on Stiff Records and again in 1987.\n- The 2009 film La Bohème is four minutes long and features images of harsh life in Ethiopia.\n- The 2009 film La Bohème is set to the duet \"O soave fanciulla\" from Puccini's opera La bohème, sung by Peter Auty and Mary Plazas.",
